{"game_id":2026020348,"away":"PHI","home":"OTT","split":{"name":"Boucher","side":1,"sec":2319},"lede":"Ottawa had last change, so Travis Green picked most of these matchups. Ottawa played without Hayden Hodgson and lost Tyler Boucher after 18:39 of the second. Philadelphia played without Michael Bunting.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"The fourth line drew Couturier’s line","text":"Travis Green sent Blais, Halliday and Boucher out for 5:43 of their 6:27 at 5-on-5 against Barkey, Couturier and Acciari (89%, about 24% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.19 to 0.15 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"Stützle’s line drew Zegras’s line","text":"Zetterlund, Stützle and Cozens spent 9:44 of their 13:14 at 5-on-5 against Foerster, Zegras and Konecny (74%, about 30% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.77 to 0.12 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Dvorak’s line","text":"Tomasino, Pinto and Batherson spent 6:18 of their 9:29 at 5-on-5 against Knuble, Dvorak and Tippett (66%, about 26% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.38 to 0.02 expected goals. Ottawa scored one of its five goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Boucher left, the lines changed and most matchups held","text":"Giroux went from 24% to 36% and Batherson from 21% to 30% of Ottawa’s 5-on-5 time, and Halliday dropped from 18% to 2%. The matchups mostly stayed: Stützle’s line against Philadelphia’s first line (71% before, 82% after) and the third line against Philadelphia’s third line (56% before, 91% after). One changed: Giroux’s line against Philadelphia’s second line (52% before, 3% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went worse","text":"Ottawa had 1.71 to 0.40 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Boucher left and 0.73 to 0.35 after. Ottawa led for most of that stretch, though, and a team ahead usually sits back, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Travis Green matched about as hard as in